      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 2.58,
          "en": "So we can now see the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 5.49,
          "en": "of our header component on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.49,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "but, of course, it doesn't really look the way I want it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 10.47,
          "en": "to look yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.47,
          "end": 13.143,
          "en": "And we can change this by adding some styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.98,
          "end": 17.43,
          "en": "which is typically done by adding a new file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.43,
          "end": 20.88,
          "en": "a header.component.css file in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.88,
          "end": 23.433,
          "en": "Again, using that same naming pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.54,
          "end": 27.39,
          "en": "and by then linking to that style file inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.39,
          "end": 29.74,
          "en": "of the header.component TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.69,
          "end": 35.55,
          "en": "by setting up the styleUrl configuration property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.55,
          "end": 39.48,
          "en": "which just like templateUrl wants a relative path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.48,
          "end": 41.313,
          "en": "to that style file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.3,
          "end": 45.663,
          "en": "So in this case, to header.component.css.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 51.98,
          "en": "By the way, there also is a styleUrls property you can set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.37,
          "end": 54.6,
          "en": "which would take an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 58.833,
          "en": "of multiple external style files that should be considered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.91,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "And there also is just a styles property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "which you could also set, which wants an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 70.68,
          "en": "of inline styles where you define the CSS styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.68,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "right inside of this TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 76.2,
          "en": "so that you could set up your CSS rules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.2,
          "end": 78.633,
          "en": "like this right inside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.49,
          "end": 83.88,
          "en": "That would work but just as with inline templates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.88,
          "end": 86.46000000000001,
          "en": "it's actually a discouraged pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.46000000000001,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "and the most common way of linking to external files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 92.25,
          "en": "is therefore with styleUrls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.25,
          "end": 96.93299999999999,
          "en": "or if it's just a single file, with styleUrl like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.19,
          "end": 100.89,
          "en": "Now, since this is not a CSS course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "we won't write the style code together though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 106.41,
          "en": "but instead, attached you find a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.41,
          "end": 109.56,
          "en": "to a header.component.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.56,
          "end": 111.87,
          "en": "which I prepared in advance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.87,
          "end": 114.42,
          "en": "which you can simply copy into your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.42,
          "end": 117.45,
          "en": "or you can copy the styles defined in that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.45,
          "end": 120.063,
          "en": "into your header.component.css file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.92,
          "end": 124.32,
          "en": "And attached, you actually also find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.32,
          "end": 126.633,
          "en": "some other assets and files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 131.61,
          "en": "For example, a task-management-logo.png file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 132.69,
          "en": "which you should copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.69,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "and paste into your assets folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 139.683,
          "en": "because we'll soon use this image in our header markup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.24,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "And you also find an updated styles.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 149.55,
          "en": "which you should use to replace your styles.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.55,
          "end": 152.523,
          "en": "which you find directly in the Ssrc folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 157.29,
          "en": "This style file sets up some global styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.29,
          "end": 160.23,
          "en": "that will apply to all components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.23,
          "end": 164.43,
          "en": "whereas the component-specific style files set up styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 168.21,
          "en": "that apply only to the components they belong to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 172.023,
          "en": "so they can't clash with styles of other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.92000000000002,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "We also need some global styles though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 179.01,
          "en": "and that's why you find an updated styles.css file attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 179.01,
          "end": 182.163,
          "en": "and you can simply replace yours with the attached one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.6,
          "end": 188.6,
          "en": "Now, this attached file also uses some special fontd,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.94,
          "end": 191.79,
          "en": "which we can import from Google Fonts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 191.79,
          "end": 196.07999999999998,
          "en": "and therefore, you should also go to the index.html file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.07999999999998,
          "end": 198.27,
          "en": "and you should replace this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.27,
          "end": 201.72,
          "en": "with the index.html file you find attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.72,
